WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.190 --> 00:00:01.210
- So you woke up this morning,

00:00:01.210 --> 00:00:02.730
you checked your crypto portfolio

00:00:02.730 --> 00:00:04.510
and (man gasping) what
happened to my crypto?

00:00:04.510 --> 00:00:06.430
- [Narrator] Lately cryptocurrency prices

00:00:06.430 --> 00:00:08.480
have been going on a wild ride

00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:11.540
and a lot of it has to do with Elon Musk.

00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:13.990
- Look, I know I sometimes
say or post strange things

00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:15.470
but that's just how my brain works.

00:00:15.470 --> 00:00:17.310
- [Narrator] The Tesla and SpaceX CEO

00:00:17.310 --> 00:00:20.480
has a lot to say about
cryptocurrencies, often on Twitter.

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:21.320
- Surprise.

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:22.700
You just got Eloned.

00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:24.360
- [Narrator] While Musk is the only thing

00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:27.200
impacting crypto prices,
one thing is clear.

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:28.920
- When he tweets about cryptocurrencies,

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:32.440
it can move markets and
that power is unparalleled.

00:00:32.440 --> 00:00:34.140
- [Narrator] Here's how Musk has amassed

00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:36.620
such influence over cryptocurrencies

00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:39.373
and why some experts are raising alarms.

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:43.290
To understand just how
influential Musk can be,

00:00:43.290 --> 00:00:44.720
take a look here.

00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:47.000
On May 12th, Bitcoin was continuing

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:49.040
on a steady downward trend,

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:51.750
running off of an all-time
high the month before.

00:00:51.750 --> 00:00:54.810
At 5 o'clock p.m., the
cryptocurrency was hovering

00:00:54.810 --> 00:00:59.810
around $55,000 and then at
6:06 p.m., this happened.

00:01:00.620 --> 00:01:03.270
Musk tweeted that his
electric vehicle company,

00:01:03.270 --> 00:01:06.440
Tesla, would no longer
accept Bitcoin as payment

00:01:06.440 --> 00:01:09.180
due to concern over rapidly increasing use

00:01:09.180 --> 00:01:12.680
of fossil fuels for Bitcoin
mining and transactions.

00:01:12.680 --> 00:01:13.940
After the tweet went out,

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:16.780
the price of Bitcoin plunged more than 5%,

00:01:16.780 --> 00:01:20.550
losing around $150 billion
by the end of the day.

00:01:20.550 --> 00:01:21.690
- After that, he did have a lot

00:01:21.690 --> 00:01:24.020
of people who were really
upset with Elon Musk.

00:01:24.020 --> 00:01:24.853
- [Narrator] Caitlin Ostroff,

00:01:24.853 --> 00:01:26.820
who has been following Musk's influence

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:29.340
on the crypto market for
The Wall Street Journal says

00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:30.700
that there's been speculation

00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:33.050
that a lot of the selling
after Elon's tweet

00:01:33.050 --> 00:01:34.930
was because retail traders weren't used

00:01:34.930 --> 00:01:36.110
to the high volatility.

00:01:36.110 --> 00:01:37.550
- People have to understand

00:01:37.550 --> 00:01:39.960
that this thing, this is a dice roll.

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:41.170
- [Narrator] They suddenly got nervous

00:01:41.170 --> 00:01:43.520
that they were going to
lose profits and sold.

00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:45.010
- They were replying to him on Twitter

00:01:45.010 --> 00:01:48.750
and they were saying you just
cost me X thousands of dollars

00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:51.930
because all of a sudden
my investment portfolio

00:01:51.930 --> 00:01:55.520
was worth 5,000 and
now it's worth maybe 4.

00:01:55.520 --> 00:01:57.600
- [Narrator] But hasn't just been Bitcoin.

00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:00.750
Musk has tweeted about other
cryptocurrencies as well.

00:02:00.750 --> 00:02:03.674
Take the once joke crypto Dogecoin.

00:02:03.674 --> 00:02:05.020
- And it keeps climbing.

00:02:05.020 --> 00:02:07.970
The meme-inspired
cryptocurrency nearly doubling

00:02:07.970 --> 00:02:09.470
over the past week alone.

00:02:09.470 --> 00:02:12.340
This ahead of Elon
Musk's appearance on SNL.

00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:13.630
- [Narrator] Early on May 8th,

00:02:13.630 --> 00:02:15.910
before Musk was slated to host an episode

00:02:15.910 --> 00:02:17.160
of "Saturday Night Live,"

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:20.030
Dogecoin was trading around 73 cents.

00:02:20.030 --> 00:02:22.957
Investors had been pumping
money into the cryptocurrency

00:02:22.957 --> 00:02:26.850
based on speculation that it
could finally reach a dollar.

00:02:26.850 --> 00:02:28.750
But that didn't happen.

00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:30.437
During a skit he performed in the guise

00:02:30.437 --> 00:02:32.250
of a financial expert,

00:02:32.250 --> 00:02:35.270
the self-proclaimed Doge
Father jokingly explained

00:02:35.270 --> 00:02:36.460
what Dogecoin is.

00:02:36.460 --> 00:02:38.710
- It's a cryptocurrency you can trade

00:02:38.710 --> 00:02:41.002
for conventional money.

00:02:41.002 --> 00:02:42.830
- Oh, so it's a hustle.

00:02:42.830 --> 00:02:44.036
- Yeah, it's a hustle.

00:02:44.036 --> 00:02:44.869
(audience laughing)

00:02:44.869 --> 00:02:45.960
- [Narrator] By the
time the episode ended,

00:02:45.960 --> 00:02:49.140
the price of the crypto
had plummeted around 30%.

00:02:49.140 --> 00:02:52.261
- That comment alone
rattled the confidence

00:02:52.261 --> 00:02:53.770
that people had that Dogecoin

00:02:53.770 --> 00:02:55.380
could keep pushing higher

00:02:55.380 --> 00:02:56.340
and people took profits

00:02:56.340 --> 00:02:57.670
and all of a sudden, it sold off.

00:02:57.670 --> 00:02:59.320
- [Narrator] But then two weeks later,

00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:02.270
Musk tweeted a picture of
a Shiba Inu on a dollar

00:03:02.270 --> 00:03:05.410
with the question how much
is that Doge in the window?

00:03:05.410 --> 00:03:08.255
Following his tweet, the price spiked.

00:03:08.255 --> 00:03:09.890
- Dogecoin, unlike Bitcoin,

00:03:09.890 --> 00:03:12.200
doesn't really have an investment case

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:13.938
and that means that Dogecoin

00:03:13.938 --> 00:03:16.880
is really just a
cryptocurrency built on memes.

00:03:16.880 --> 00:03:20.070
The only reason it has any
value at all at the moment

00:03:20.070 --> 00:03:22.970
is because Elon Musk first
started caring about it

00:03:22.970 --> 00:03:25.350
and then Snoop Dogg
started caring about it.

00:03:25.350 --> 00:03:27.240
And then all of these other rappers

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:30.060
and celebrities starting
tweeting about Dogecoin.

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:32.350
- [Narrator] While these are
two of the most recent examples

00:03:32.350 --> 00:03:35.330
of Musk influencing crypto,
there are many more.

00:03:35.330 --> 00:03:37.260
And there are other forces at play

00:03:37.260 --> 00:03:38.240
that have allowed Musk

00:03:38.240 --> 00:03:40.510
to amass the influence he has on crypto.

00:03:40.510 --> 00:03:41.700
Over the last year,

00:03:41.700 --> 00:03:44.310
there has been a flood
of new retail investors,

00:03:44.310 --> 00:03:45.990
largely driven by the rise

00:03:45.990 --> 00:03:48.840
in no-fee trading apps, like Robhinhood.

00:03:48.840 --> 00:03:50.480
Meltem Demirors, an executive

00:03:50.480 --> 00:03:53.110
at the asset management firm CoinShares

00:03:53.110 --> 00:03:54.690
says that no-fee trading apps

00:03:54.690 --> 00:03:56.770
have increased the popularity of crypto

00:03:56.770 --> 00:03:59.310
because people can access
more types of assets

00:03:59.310 --> 00:04:00.710
on the same platform.

00:04:00.710 --> 00:04:03.380
- It's also made really
illiquid cryptocurrencies

00:04:03.380 --> 00:04:05.710
of the past much more liquid

00:04:05.710 --> 00:04:08.190
because there's now much
more retail participation.

00:04:08.190 --> 00:04:10.290
- [Narrator] Some experts
say younger people gravitate

00:04:10.290 --> 00:04:12.320
towards Musk because they like his idea

00:04:12.320 --> 00:04:14.600
of the future and see him as rebellious.

00:04:14.600 --> 00:04:17.200
And Demirors says Musk's
huge Twitter following

00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:19.100
is a big part of his influence.

00:04:19.100 --> 00:04:21.540
He has over 56 million followers.

00:04:21.540 --> 00:04:23.760
- Financial markets, to some people,

00:04:23.760 --> 00:04:25.900
are a form of entertainment

00:04:25.900 --> 00:04:27.600
and so I think what we are seeing

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:31.120
is the gamification of
clout on social media

00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:32.285
where people are recognizing

00:04:32.285 --> 00:04:35.810
that they can manipulate
markets using social media

00:04:35.810 --> 00:04:36.643
as a tool.

00:04:36.643 --> 00:04:38.350
- [Narrator] but she says Musk's influence

00:04:38.350 --> 00:04:40.350
on the crypto market has downsides.

00:04:40.350 --> 00:04:41.870
- There is a wide range of ways

00:04:41.870 --> 00:04:43.240
through which market participants

00:04:43.240 --> 00:04:47.760
are acting on their desire to
buy and sell cryptocurrencies

00:04:47.760 --> 00:04:48.790
and as a result,

00:04:48.790 --> 00:04:51.210
we see is more liquidity

00:04:51.210 --> 00:04:53.040
but also more volatility

00:04:53.040 --> 00:04:54.620
when people like the Elon Musk

00:04:54.620 --> 00:04:56.920
are tweeting directly to retail.

00:04:56.920 --> 00:04:59.260
- [Narrator] All assets are
subject to ups and downs

00:04:59.260 --> 00:05:02.050
but as you can see from the
big swings on this chart,

00:05:02.050 --> 00:05:03.940
crypto's especially volatile.

00:05:03.940 --> 00:05:06.040
- All of a sudden, Elon
has reminded people no,

00:05:06.040 --> 00:05:08.260
this isn't just going
up in a straight line,

00:05:08.260 --> 00:05:11.210
it does come down and when
it does, it can be fast.

00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:12.290
- [Narrator] These market swings

00:05:12.290 --> 00:05:15.220
can have a very real
impact on retail investors

00:05:15.220 --> 00:05:17.380
but for some, the risk is worth.

00:05:17.380 --> 00:05:18.800
- Because there's no fundamentals,

00:05:18.800 --> 00:05:20.160
it makes it really hard

00:05:20.160 --> 00:05:22.010
to try and figure out where the floor is,

00:05:22.010 --> 00:05:23.580
like where the fair value

00:05:23.580 --> 00:05:26.570
and where the selloff
should stop when it happens.

00:05:26.570 --> 00:05:28.780
And so you inherently wind up having

00:05:28.780 --> 00:05:30.640
a much more volatile market,

00:05:30.640 --> 00:05:33.670
which is what appeals to
some investors for this.

00:05:33.670 --> 00:05:35.340
They don't want the steady returns

00:05:35.340 --> 00:05:38.430
of the S&amp;P where they
have to wait 30 years

00:05:38.430 --> 00:05:40.150
to get where they wanna be.

00:05:40.150 --> 00:05:43.360
They want to get these
fast, sharp returns.

00:05:43.360 --> 00:05:45.540
- [Narrator] Some experts
think that Musk's influence

00:05:45.540 --> 00:05:47.260
on Bitcoin may be waning.

00:05:47.260 --> 00:05:49.260
But for now, his tweets continue

00:05:49.260 --> 00:05:51.339
to send shock waves
through the crypto market.

00:05:51.339 --> 00:05:54.006
(pensive music)

